{
  "id": "M36",
  "classification": "retained network identity, distance and travel-duration producer migration gap; no ordinary routing arithmetic failure asserted",
  "title": "Carry network identities and exact route quantities through graph operations",
  "locations": [
    {
      "file": "crates/adventuresim-world-import/src/draft.rs",
      "start": 35,
      "end": 45
    },
    {
      "file": "crates/adventuresim-world-import/src/sources/viabundus/mod.rs",
      "start": 367,
      "end": 380
    },
    {
      "file": "crates/adventuresim-world-import/src/sources/road_inference.rs",
      "start": 207,
      "end": 240
    },
    {
      "file": "crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/travel_planning.rs",
      "start": 55,
      "end": 119
    },
    {
      "file": "crates/adventuresim-core/src/reputation.rs",
      "start": 22,
      "end": 42
    }
  ],
  "contract_trace": "CSV node/edge IDs and lengths are decoded to interchangeable u64/u32 values retained by SourceNode, TravelEdgeDraft and graph records. They flow through inferred-road candidate/adjacency/shortest-path state, compiled import DTOs and native tables into travel_neighbors, connected_settlement_distances, reputation propagation and bounded public-threat hearing. Internal maps and positional neighbor pairs do not distinguish node IDs from edge IDs or accumulated metres from IDs/time. journey_minutes and quest_journey_minutes convert a raw u64 distance into another raw u64 subsequently used as planned movement time. Actual CSV, reducer JSON, table indexes and hashing bytes are terminal/native requirements; intermediate planning graphs and route/time records are application state.",
  "repair": "Establish shared network node/edge identity owners and exact integer metric-distance leaves at source admission, retaining them in internal drafts, graphs and receiving calculations. Use a named neighbor/route-cost record. Preserve u32 edge representation where required and full u64 accumulated metres, with explicit checked or saturating operations matching the current policy. Return a relative planned-travel duration owner, separate from StrategicMinute absolute clocks and from positive RequestedDuration where a zero result is valid. Keep codecs at actual CSV/JSON/index/hash ports instead of using transport DTOs as unchecked internal state. Reconcile all reputation, hearing and journey consumers with the same owners. Reuse frame-neutral geometry concepts only where precision/sign/zero policies fit; f32 PositiveLength/SignedLength are not lossless replacements for arbitrary u64 integer metres. Do not substitute structural/artillery node IDs or bounded water-distance types.",
  "dependencies": [
    "M32 reputation and M34 public-threat hearing reuse the same network node/distance concepts",
    "M35 population and source-node absence remain separate roles; demo settlements deliberately have no imported node",
    "M37 journey place/frame contracts share travel planning/reducers and require one reconciled function repair",
    "Remaining route-terrain, importer validation/builder, journey/camp and encounter consumers need full source coverage before completion"
  ],
  "acceptance": "Native ID bit patterns, inferred high-bit namespace and collision handling remain unchanged; no unsupported global nonzero-ID restriction. Preserve positive edge-length admission, zero accumulated origin distance, native integer precision, stable route order, next-settlement stopping, finite graph bounds where specified, checked/saturating accumulation, ceil duration conversion, minimum-one ordinary journey and deliberate zero-distance case-site arrival. Actual JSON/index/hash representations remain explicit codecs. The same owners cross every connected internal producer/state/receiver; no primitive adapters preserve old APIs. Existing tests only, none added or run; family and other-lens acceptance remain incomplete."
}
